Unless a file states otherwise, this repository uses two licenses:

1. Documentation is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (`CC-BY-4.0`). This includes Markdown and other documentation under `docs/`, `integrations/`, and `governance/`, plus the root project documentation. See `LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0`.
2. Source code, JSON Schema, fixtures, executable examples, tests, and build or automation files are licensed under Apache License 2.0 (`Apache-2.0`). This includes code and related assets under `code/`, executable implementation files under `integrations/`, and files under `scripts/` and `.github/`. See `LICENSE-APACHE-2.0`.

When a directory contains both documentation and code, the file type and an explicit per-file notice take precedence over the directory default. Third-party dependencies and linked external projects remain under their own licenses.

No additional contributor agreement or sign-off is currently required. By submitting a contribution, contributors represent that they have the right to submit it and agree that accepted contributions are distributed under the license applicable to the contributed file or directory. See `CONTRIBUTING.md`.
